From 422a05ae5db8303f44a07f33e33f6eb2883cae00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Laroche <larochealexandre@hotmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:12:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] statem_srvr.c: clear the freed inner ClientHello pointer in
 tls_process_client_hello()

On the ECH backend path, s->ext.ech.innerch was freed, but the pointer
to it was kept until the buffer replacing it was allocated.  An error
condition in between could lead to a jump to err:, where a second attempt
to free s->ext.ech.innerch could be made.  The only such error today,
the PACKET_peek_bytes() of PACKET_remaining() bytes, cannot happen,
but the pointer should not outlive the buffer.

Complements: 6c3edd4f3a8a "Add server-side handling of Encrypted Client Hello"
Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Reviewed-by: Milan Broz <gmazyland@gmail.com>
Reviewed-by: Eugene Syromiatnikov <esyr@openssl.org>
Merge-date: Fri Nov 20 14:19:23 2026
Merged-from: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33705
(cherry picked from commit 21d4b79c0b9c8a585e226cf3cc4e228affc3e2d3)
---
 ssl/statem/statem_srvr.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/ssl/statem/statem_srvr.c b/ssl/statem/statem_srvr.c
index 13f1ee4..1b871ba 100644
--- a/ssl/statem/statem_srvr.c
+++ b/ssl/statem/statem_srvr.c
@@ -2066,6 +2066,7 @@ MSG_PROCESS_RETURN tls_process_client_hello(SSL_CONNECTION *s, PACKET *pkt)
             s->ext.ech.backend = 1;
             s->ext.ech.attempted_type = TLSEXT_TYPE_ech;
             OPENSSL_free(s->ext.ech.innerch);
+            s->ext.ech.innerch = NULL;
             s->ext.ech.innerch_len = PACKET_remaining(pkt);
             if (PACKET_peek_bytes(pkt, &pbuf, s->ext.ech.innerch_len) != 1) {
                 SSLfatal(s, SSL_AD_INTERNAL_ERROR, ERR_R_INTERNAL_ERROR);
-- 
